  // ======================================================================
  // 4. swell (chosen): one swell crosses the page from right to left, the homepage ahead of it, the sign-in page
  //    behind it. One thing travels: the headline and its line, carried on the crest as a line that bobs a little
  //    on the water and reads the whole way, shrinking and setting down at the bottom left as the crest comes to
  //    rest. Everything else stays itself: the homepage goes under with the crest, the sign-in page is revealed
  //    whole behind it, and only the form's title decodes once, as the entrance does. Both pages are one sea at
  //    one scale; the panel simply covers its right. It moves the moment you press: fast at first, then easing
  //    to rest, about 1.1 s, and everything lands together. Turning round midway sends it back the way it came.
